# Document previews

Whenever a document is created, sent, attached, or shown in the CRM (quotes, invoices, PDFs, mail attachments, email HTML), the user must see an **inline preview** — not only a filename, download chip, or “Open” link.

## Required behavior

- Mail/chat attachments: render an inline preview in the bubble (PDF pages, image, text body, or iframe/`object` embed). Never ship header-only attachment rows for previewable files.
- Quotes/invoices: keep the existing preview modal/document view wired and opening correctly; PDF attachments saved to chat history must use `application/pdf` so the canvas preview runs.
- Newsletter/email editors: the live preview iframe (or equivalent) must reflect the document the user is editing.
- If a format cannot be rendered natively, still show a visible preview panel (embed attempt + clear fallback), not an empty gap.

## Do not

- Leave documents as download-only when a preview path already exists in the codebase (`MessageAttachments`, `QuoteDocument`, `InvoiceDocument`, mailing preview iframe).
- Save quote/invoice PDFs without persisting them as reply attachments with a PDF mime type.
